      "side": 1,
      "message": "Right, this does not handle it. Only the endpoint itself is registered for removal, so a bridge going away takes its own device offline but leaves the devices behind it polling a dead EID. Handling them needs mctpd to rediscover bridged endpoints first, which it does not yet do\n(https://github.com/CodeConstruct/mctp/issues/149), so I would rather do it as its own change once that lands than half-do it here.",
      "parentUuid": "564dacdc_0eb4424e",
